comments.body:
Hi! It depends on which version you're on. `orbit doctor` prints it on the first line. Right now
the latest release is 2.8.0, and 2.9 is planned as the last 2.x release. Generally:

- if you're on 2.x, staying current within 2.x is recommended (bug and security fixes);
- read `changelog` for anything that affects you before upgrading;
- 3.0 will be a bigger change (new config file), so plan that one separately.

If you tell us your version and broker we can give a more specific answer.
